<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>Fabricator.Bridge</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Fabricator.Common</AssemblyName>
    <Description>
      The reusable middle: dependency-light IMPLEMENTATIONS of the Fabricator.Abstractions contracts that a
      provider or plugin would otherwise hand-roll - Arrow value reading, the Arrow stream adapters, the
      custom-aggregate session, and the fixed-schema function base classes. Kept in the Fabricator.Bridge
      namespace (assembly split only - no source churn), exactly as Fabricator.Abstractions and
      Fabricator.Delta are.

      OPTIONAL for a plugin, which is the whole point: it references Abstractions (+ Apache.Arrow) and
      nothing else, so taking it on adds no package to a plugin's closure. It must NEVER reference
      Fabricator.Bridge - Bridge references THIS, so a reference back is a project cycle, and that
      impossibility is the membership rule: a type that needs the running host cannot live here, it is a
      SERVICE (see FabricatorServices). docs/plugin-services.md sections 6 and 7.4.
    </Description>

    <!-- PACKABLE. Directory.Build.props turns packing OFF for the whole folder; these two assemblies are the
         only ones a plugin may reference, so they are the only ones that opt back in.
         /!\ PackageId is UNRESERVED on nuget.org: `Fabricator.Abstractions` is free but the bare `Fabricator`
         ID is TAKEN by an unrelated package (checked 2026-09-02), so a `Fabricator.*` prefix reservation is
         unlikely to be granted. That binds nothing while packages go to a local folder or a release asset;
         revisit the ID before publishing to nuget.org. docs/plugin-services.md section 5 Q4. -->
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>Fabricator.Common</PackageId>
    <PackageDescription>Optional reusable implementations of the Fabricator.Abstractions contracts - Arrow value reading, the Arrow stream adapters, the custom-aggregate session, and the fixed-schema function base classes - so a plugin need not hand-roll them. Adds no package to a plugin closure beyond Abstractions.</PackageDescription>
    <PackageTags>duckdb;fabricator;plugin;arrow</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Abstractions ONLY. Apache.Arrow arrives with it. Adding any other package here is a change to every
         plugin's compile closure, which is the cost this assembly exists to avoid. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Fabricator.Abstractions\Fabricator.Abstractions.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
